  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 815-20-25, natural hedging involves matching foreign currency inflows with outflows in the same currency to reduce net exposure without derivative instruments. Global Parts already has EUR 2 million in receivables offset by EUR 1.5 million in payables, reducing net exposure to EUR 500,000 through operational alignment.
Wrong (A): Forward contracts hedge exposure but involve counterparty risk and transaction costs, and do not reduce the underlying net exposure through operational means.
Wrong (B): Currency options provide protection but require premium payments and address symptoms rather than structurally reducing the exposure.
Wrong (D): Converting all operations to USD is impractical for a company with existing euro-denominated business relationships and contracts.$EXPL$
